    "https://jobmarket.unibocconi.eu/?id=1005": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Dept. Finance",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/11/2026 Posted Date: 14/10/2026 Department: Finance  Via Sarfatti, 25 - 20136 Milano, Italia unibocconi.it Academic Positions (3) at Assistant Professor of Finance (tenure-track) Finance Department - Bocconi University - Milan The Department of Finance at Bocconi University invites applications for three full-time faculty positions at the Assistant Professor level in the Department of Finance, starting September 1, 2027. The positions are open to candidates working in all fields of Finance. Junior candidates are hired to an eight-year tenure-track position, with a mid -term review and the possibility of promotion to tenured Associate Professor before the end of the eight- year period. Job Qualifications: Candidates should show considerable promise for excellent research and teaching. Applicants should be nearing the completion of their Ph.D. in Finance, Economics, or related fields, or should have already completed it. Salary for Assistant professors in Finance starts from €120,000. The final salary offer may be adjusted according to the actual seniority of the successful candidate, in accordance with the objective and non-discriminatory criteria adopted by the university. Application Procedure: Applications must be submitted online at: https://jobmarket.unibocconi.eu/?id=1005 The deadline to submit your package is 15th November, 2026 (11:59 PM, Italian time). All applications should include a cover letter, a complete CV which includes a list of publications, a job market paper, a research statement, and the names and contact details of three referees of high academic standing. Referees will automatically receive an email with instructions to upload their letters directly. For clarifications or questions with the application, please contact faculty@unibocconi.it. Interviews will be held virtually, and selected candidates will be invited for in-person flyouts. Bocconi University is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty. Applications are particularly welcome from women and members of groups who are under -represented in academic posts. About the Organization: Bocconi University is a leading European university. It is located in central Milan, Italy, offering undergraduate, graduate, PhD, MBA and Executive programs in finance, economics, management and law. Bocconi is a private university and fully independent f rom the public university system. It is the leading school for finance and economics education in Italy, with strong ties to the financial and industrial community, in Italy and abroad. "
    },
    "https://jobmarket.unibocconi.eu/?id=1008": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Dept. Decision Sciences",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/12/2026 Posted Date: 14/10/2026 Department: Decision Sciences  Via Sarfatti, 25 - 20136 Milano, Italia unibocconi.it ASSISTANT PROFESSOR IN MATHEMATICS Department of Decision Sciences, Bocconi University, Milan, Italy Description The Department of Decision Sciences of Bocconi University in Milan, invites applications for a Tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level in Mathematical Analysis, with a focus on one of the topical modern areas, including e.g. partial differential equations, calculus of variations and geometric measure theory, geometric analysis and Riemannian geometry, dynamical systems, harmonic and stochastic analysis, and possibly their applications, in particular in economics, optimization, control and machine learning. The appointment will begin in Fall 2027. The Department of Decision Sciences is an amazingly vibrant academic community in the fields of Mathematical Analysis, Statistics, and Theoretical Economics, with strong interactions with outstanding research groups in Optimization, Machine Learning, and Computing Sciences. Qualifications Applicants should have, or be close to completing, a Ph.D. and demonstrate high research potential. Job information Successful candidates will be expected to develop a strong publication record, contribute to the academic life of the department, and be effective teachers both at the undergraduate and graduate level, in particular for the new BSc program in Mathematical and Computing Sciences for Artificial Intelligence. Compensation and teaching load will be competitive with other top European Schools. The tenure track will run for up to eight years (with one paid sabbatical year ). There is the possibility of promotion to a tenured position by the end of that period or before. For additional information concerning the Department of Decision Sciences visit https://dec.unibocconi.eu/ Further details on the position may be requested from faculty@unibocconi.it How to apply Applications using the on-line application form, must be sent electronically via the site www.unibocconi.eu/jobmarket by 23:59 of December 15th, 2026 (Italian time). The following documents must be attached to the electronic application: a. a scientific curriculum (including a list of publications); Via Sarfatti, 25 - 20136 Milano, Italia unibocconi.it b. the (up to) three most relevant publications of the candidate; c. Three highly qualified academic referees who will provide a reference letter. Note that reference letters must also be received by the application deadline. It is therefore recommended completing the application early enough to allow time for the referees to upload their letters before the final deadline. For any problems with the online application system, candidates can contact faculty@unibocconi.it Closing date The review of applications will begin on November 16, 2026 and continue until this position is filled, the ultimate deadline for applications is December 15, 2026. Bocconi University is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty. Applications are particularly welcomed from women or members of groups who are under -represented in academic posts. "
    },
    "https://jobmarket.unibocconi.eu/?id=1007": {
      "title": "Full Professor, All Departments",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/11/2026 Posted Date: 13/10/2026  Via Sarfatti, 25 - 20136 Milano, Italia - P.IVA/ VAT n. IT03628350153 unibocconi.it 10 Full / Associate Professor Positions at SDA Bocconi School of Management Call for Applications As part of its Strategic Faculty Plan, SDA Bocconi School of Management invites applications for 10 Full or Associate Professor positions, starting September 2027. The successful candidates will hold a joint appointment with both Bocconi University Departments (i.e., Accounting, Computing Sciences, Cognitive Sciences, Economics, Finance, Management & Technology, Marketing, Decision Sciences, Legal Studies, Social and Political Sciences) and the SDA Bocconi School of Management. These positions are designed to strengthen the connection between academic and applied research and to position new Professors as leading contributors to the broader Bocconi ecosystem. The senior faculty positions represent a strategic investment in the School's intellectual leadership and future. SDA Bocconi seeks outstanding scholars with at least 3 years’ experience as tenured Associate or Full Professor s, who combine internationally recognized academic excellence with an exceptional ability to engage, challenge and inspire experienced executives and organizational leaders. We are particularly interested in professors who can contribute not only through thei r own scholarship and teaching, but also through the development of people, ideas and institutions. Through these appointments, SDA Bocconi aims to strengthen its position as a global meeting point for frontier research, transformative executive learning and responsible leadership. We are particularly interested in professors who see research excellence and educational impact as mutually reinforcing. Their research should have the potential to shape both academic thinking and managerial practice across corporations, financial institutions and government organizations , while their teaching should connect intellectual depth and frontier knowledge with the evolving realities of management and leadership. The Profile We Seek Candidates should have a scholarly record consistent with appointment at the Full or Associate Professor level and an established international reputation in their field. We are looking for scholars who combine sustained, original and influential research with intellectual leadership, international visibility, a strong entrepreneurial attitude, a recognized capability to lead high- level executive education projects and a strong commitment to developing younger scholars. Beyond their individual achievements, successful candidates will be expected to act as institution builders and academic leaders. They should have a proven ability and genuine commitment to developing the next generation of scholars and professors: mentoring younger faculty, creating opportunities for intellectual growth, fostering a culture of excellence and helping promising academics develop into internationally recognized, world-class professors in their own right. This commitment to developing people should extend beyond individual mentorship. Full and Associate Professors will be expected to contribute actively to the intellectual and institutional development of SDA Bocconi, building: applied research platforms, executive education initiatives, partnerships and academic communities where appropriate. They shoul d have the ambition and capacity to shape the School's future faculty, strengthen its intellectual community and leave a lasting institutional legacy. The ideal candidates will also bring: • excellence in teaching (at executive masters, MBA and executive education level) and mentoring, particularly with senior and experienced participants; • the ability to translate sophisticated research into relevant and engaging executive learning; • a strong understanding of the challenges facing contemporary organizations and leaders; • the ability to translate research into meaningful engagement with companies, institutions, policymakers and broader society; • a global perspective and an openness to interdisciplinary collaboration; • an interest in developing new research and executive initiatives and building intellectual communities; • a commitment to responsible leadership and to creating positive impact for individuals, organizations and society. The search encompasses major fields of Bocconi University Departments, with a special focus on topics relevant for the School, such as corporate finance and banking, corporate strategy, leadership, corporate governance and family business, marketing, entrepreneurship, innovation, technology, geopolitics, as well as public management. Application details: Candidates are asked to send a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research statement and teaching statement showing courses they have taught, with particular emphasis on teaching experience in MBA, Executive Master and Executive Programs, as well as on any responsibilities they have had in designing executive education programs more broadly through our online application here: https:/ /jobmarket.unibocconi.eu/?id=1007 Applications must be received by: 30 November 2026 and candidates will be invited for fly-outs starting from December 2026. Why SDA Bocconi SDA Bocconi is the School of Management of Bocconi University and an international community of faculty, participants, alumni, executives and organizations. Its portfolio spans MBA and Executive MBA programs, specialized and executive Master's programs, op en-enrollment executive education, and customized programs developed with companies and institutions where the leading position of the School is globally recognized by major rankings. This breadth creates a distinctive environment for senior scholars. Research can inform multiple forms of education, while continuous engagement with leaders and organizations can generate new questions, perspectives and opportunities for research. Joint a ppointments with Bocconi University Departments further connect faculty to a broader academic ecosystem and create opportunities to bridge disciplinary scholarship with management practice. The School encourages faculty to engage with the forces reshaping management and society —from the evolution of finance, ownership and governance to artificial intelligence and the future of work, geopolitical fragmentation, demographic change, and new forms of entrepreneurship and innovation. For senior scholars who aspire to have an impact beyond their individual research portfolios, SDA Bocconi offers the opportunity to shape ideas, develop people, build institutions and contribute to the future of management education and research. What SDA Bocconi Offers SDA Bocconi offers Full and Associate Professors an internationally competitive package designed to support academic excellence, intellectual leadership and meaningful engagement with executives, organizations and institutions. Full and Associate Professors will be affiliated to a Bocconi Department but most of their activity overall will be devoted to SDA Bocconi. The package typically includes: • internationally competitive compensation which will depend on the profile and experience of the candidate • a comprehensive range of benefits, healthcare insurance plan and relocation services; • an annual budget to support research, conferences and dissemination activities; • access to SDA Bocconi's international community of executives, organizations, alumni and faculty; • opportunities to develop new research, educational and institutional initiatives; • a world-class campus in Milan. Bocconi University is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty. Applications are particularly welcomed from women or members of groups who are under-represented in academic posts. "
    }
  },
